36. IMPORTANT INTERVIEW DIFFERENCES
============================================================

git fetch vs git pull

FETCH:
Downloads changes only.

PULL:
Downloads and integrates changes.


git merge vs git rebase

MERGE:
Combines histories and normally creates a merge commit.

REBASE:
Replays commits on a new base and creates a linear history.


git reset vs git revert

RESET:
Rewrites/moves history.

REVERT:
Creates a new commit that reverses previous changes.


git pull vs git pull --rebase

PULL:
Usually fetch + merge.

PULL --REBASE:
Fetch + replay local commits on top of remote changes.


git add vs git commit

ADD:
Moves changes to staging.

COMMIT:
Saves staged changes into Git history.


